From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium meta-browser maintainers <meta-browser@lists.openembedded.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v8: disable concurrent mksnapshot under QEMU

The arm64 mksnapshot binary is executed through QEMU when Chromium is
cross-compiled on a different host architecture. Concurrent builtin
generation currently aborts with SIGTRAP in this configuration. Use the
serial snapshot path so the build-time generator can complete reliably.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 v8/BUILD.gn | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/BUILD.gn b/v8/BUILD.gn
--- a/v8/BUILD.gn
+++ b/v8/BUILD.gn
@@ -137,0 +138,5 @@
+
+  # mksnapshot is executed through QEMU for cross-architecture builds.
+  if (is_linux && current_cpu == "arm64" && host_cpu != "arm64") {
+    v8_enable_concurrent_mksnapshot = false
+  }
-- 
